# Color Usage Rules for Next.js

## 🎯 Precise Usage Rules: Tailwind vs Modus vs Design System

### The Three Systems Working Together

**1. Tailwind CSS** → Layout, spacing, typography, responsive design
**2. Design System Colors** → Mapped colors for custom UI (via Tailwind classes)
**3. Modus Web Components** → Pre-built components with color props

### 📝 Complete Example Showing All Three Systems

```tsx
import { ModusWcButton } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";

export default function ProductCard() {
  return (
    {/* Tailwind: layout, spacing, responsive */}
    <div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-4 p-6 rounded-lg border transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-lg bg-card border-border">

      {/* Tailwind: typography, spacing */}
      {/* Design System: text color */}
      <div className="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">
        Product Name
      </div>

      {/* Tailwind: typography */}
      {/* Design System: muted text color */}
      <div className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Product description
      </div>

      {/* Tailwind: layout, spacing, hover states */}
      {/* Design System: colors */}
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">
        Custom Button
      </ModusWcButton>

      {/* Modus Web Component: uses color props */}
      <ModusWcButton color="primary" variant="filled">
        Modus Button
      </ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Breakdown:**

- **Tailwind** handles: `flex`, `gap-4`, `p-6`, `rounded-lg`, `text-lg`, `hover:shadow-lg`
- **Design System** handles: `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`
- **Modus Components** use: `color="primary"`, `variant="filled"`

### ✅ What to Use When

| **Use Case**           | **What to Use**       | **Example**                                            |
| ---------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Layout**             | Tailwind classes      | `flex`, `grid`, `items-center`, `gap-4`                |
| **Spacing**            | Tailwind classes      | `p-4`, `m-2`, `px-8`, `py-6`                           |
| **Typography**         | Tailwind classes      | `text-lg`, `font-semibold`, `leading-relaxed`          |
| **Responsive**         | Tailwind classes      | `md:flex-row`, `lg:grid-cols-3`                        |
| **Transitions**        | Tailwind classes      | `transition-colors`, `duration-200`, `hover:shadow-lg` |
| **Colors (Custom UI)** | Design system classes | `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`    |
| **Hover States**       | Tailwind prefixes     | `hover:bg-card`, `hover:opacity-80`                    |
| **Focus States**       | Tailwind prefixes     | `focus:ring-2`, `focus:ring-ring`                      |
| **Modus Components**   | Color props           | `color="primary"`, `variant="filled"`                  |

### 🎨 Design System Colors (Available as Tailwind Classes)

Our design system maps Modus variables to easy-to-use Tailwind classes:

**Background Colors:**

```tsx
bg - background; // Page background
bg - card; // Card/section background
bg - muted; // Subtle background
bg - primary; // Primary brand color
bg - secondary; // Secondary color
bg - destructive; // Error/danger background
```

**Text Colors:**

```tsx
text - foreground; // Primary text
text - muted - foreground; // Subtle text
text - primary; // Primary text
text - primary - foreground; // Text on primary background
text - destructive; // Error text
```

**Border Colors:**

```tsx
border - border; // Standard borders
border - input; // Input borders
border - ring; // Focus rings
```

**Interactive States:**

```tsx
hover:bg-card              // Hover background
hover:opacity-80           // Hover opacity
focus:ring-2 focus:ring-ring  // Focus ring
```

### 🚫 DO NOT Use Raw Modus CSS Variables

**❌ Don't access Modus variables directly:**

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG - Raw Modus variables
style={{ backgroundColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)" }}
style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)" }}
style={{ borderColor: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)" }}
```

**✅ Use design system classes instead:**

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Design system classes
className = "bg-background text-foreground border-border";
```

### 📋 Original Modus Colors (For Reference Only)

These are the underlying Modus variables that power our design system. **You should NOT use these directly** - use the design system classes above instead.

**Base Colors (5 total):**

```css
var(--modus-wc-color-base-page)     /* #fff → #000 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-100)      /* #f1f1f6 → #252a2e */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-200)      /* #cbcdd6 → #464b52 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-300)      /* #b7b9c3 → #353a40 */
var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)  /* #171c1e → #cbcdd6 */
```

**Semantic Colors (4 total):**

```css
var(--modus-wc-color-info)          /* #0063a3 */
var(--modus-wc-color-success)       /* #1e8a44 */
var(--modus-wc-color-error)         /* #da212c */
var(--modus-wc-color-warning)       /* #fbad26 */
```

**Mapping to Design System:**

- `--modus-wc-color-base-page` → `bg-background`
- `--modus-wc-color-base-content` → `text-foreground`
- `--modus-wc-color-base-100` → `bg-card`
- `--modus-wc-color-base-200` → `border-border`
- `--modus-wc-color-info` → `bg-primary`
- `--modus-wc-color-error` → `bg-destructive`
- `--modus-wc-color-success` → `bg-success`
- `--modus-wc-color-warning` → `bg-warning`

### 🎯 Next.js Color Usage Patterns

#### ✅ BEST Practice: Tailwind Classes with Design System Colors

**This is the preferred approach** - uses Tailwind utility classes with our design system colors:

```tsx
// ✅ BEST - Pure Tailwind with design system colors
export default function Component() {
  return (
    <div className="p-6 bg-background border border-border text-foreground rounded-lg">
      <div className="bg-card p-4 rounded-lg hover:bg-card/90 transition-colors">
        <div className="text-foreground text-lg font-semibold">Title</div>
        <div className="text-muted-foreground">Description</div>
      </div>

      {/* Modus Web Components still use color props */}
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">Primary Button</ModusWcButton>
      <ModusWcButton color="secondary">Secondary Button</ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Why this is better:**

- ✅ No custom CSS needed
- ✅ Self-documenting (all styling visible)
- ✅ Tailwind purges unused classes automatically
- ✅ Better DX (no file jumping)
- ✅ Scalable (won't bloat `globals.css`)

#### ⚠️ Acceptable: Inline Styles (Only for Dynamic Values)

Use inline styles ONLY when values are computed/dynamic:

```tsx
export default function Component({ isActive }) {
  return (
    <div
      className="p-6"
      style={{
        backgroundColor: isActive ? "var(--primary)" : "var(--background)",
        // Only use inline styles for dynamic values
      }}
    >
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">Primary Button</ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### ❌ Avoid: CSS Modules (Legacy Approach)

CSS Modules add unnecessary complexity. Use Tailwind instead:

```tsx
// ❌ DON'T DO THIS - Unnecessary CSS module
import styles from "./Component.module.css";

export default function Component() {
  return (
    <div className={styles.component}>
      <ModusWcButton color="primary">Primary Button</ModusWcButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
/* ❌ DON'T CREATE THIS - Use Tailwind instead */
.component {
  background-color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-page);
  border: 1px solid var(--modus-wc-color-base-200);
  color: var(--modus-wc-color-base-content);
}
```

